  "title": "Distinguish links to a thread from links to a specific post?",
  "content": "<p>Currently a link to the top of a thread will give exactly the same preview as a link to a specific reply within that thread; eg, see <a href=\"https://community.st.com/stm32-mcus-embedded-software-32/stm32f051c8t6-pwm-not-generating-on-custom-tig-control-board-167326?postid=745952#post745952\" target=\"_self\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow ugc\">here</a>:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/c71fbcfa-93ba-4131-ac04-0a556a6925d5.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>I think it would be helpful if the preview made some distinction ?</p>",
